          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What are the options for that?",
          "answer": "The guidance I retrieved does not list the preventive treatment options for migraine. The national headache guidance (*Migraine: acute treatment, when prevention starts, and medication-overuse limits*) explains when prevention is considered, but the passage I received cuts off before naming any options. The part that did come through lists heart-related medicines, which are not migraine treatments, so I have not used it.\n\nOther documents in the search covered anxiety, cholesterol, heart disease and osteoarthritis. None of them answers your question about migraine.\n\nA clinician can go through the preventive options with you and explain which might suit your situation. Useful questions to bring include how disabling your attacks are, what you have already tried, and how you would know whether a treatment is working.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
